    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAS3//IOc\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/base64_utils.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 50,
      "author": {
        "id": 5046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-03T20:59:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the interest of future planning and possibly moving this to Oslo, it might be helpful to have this whole change contained within a directory specific to base64 operations. This will be helpful because then in Oslo it can be treated as a module as well (e.g. see the openstack/common/rpc/* or openstack/common/notifier/* modules for examples). Then when that times comes it would be easier to just move a directory instead of moving several modules underneath /keystone/common/. \n\nThis might also be helpful if we want to move InvalidBase64Error to its own module (/keystone/common/base64utils/exceptions.py for instance, making it easier to add new exceptions if/when this all develops. This makes things easier to find and reference when they are all in one place, and also follow structure similar to other openstack projects. \n\nJust a couple thoughts.",
      "revId": "917eb0665fa8e391fb58daf28438cab010d5a606",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAATH//INI\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/base64_utils.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 50,
      "author": {
        "id": 8116
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-10-25T16:17:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see the value in moving these to a subdirectory with the intent of moving to oslo, most of the simple oslo common utilities are currently contained in single files, e.g.\n\nauthutils.py\ncliutils.py\nexcutils.py\nfileutils.py\nfuncutils.py\ngettextutils.py\nimportutils.py\njsonutils.py\nlockutils.py\nnetwork_utils.py\nprocessutils.py\nsslutils.py\nstrutils.py\ntimeutils.py\nuuidutils.py\nxmlutils.py\n\nI do notice I have an underscore in my filenames which is not consistent with the olso common naming, I\u0027ll fix that.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAS3//IOc\u003d",
      "revId": "917eb0665fa8e391fb58daf28438cab010d5a606",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
