      "writtenOn": "2013-10-25T16:17:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It does. From the Python re module doc: When the UNICODE flag is not specified, it (\\s)  matches any whitespace character, this is equivalent to the set [ \\t\\n\\r\\f\\v]. Note, it is not necessary to use the re.MULTILINE flag here either since there are no ^ or $ anchors in the regexp.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAATH//dO0\u003d",
      "revId": "917eb0665fa8e391fb58daf28438cab010d5a606",
